## Third-party APIs

Each API of the definition has a client in `src/shared/api/<api>/`:
the TypeScript types of its schemas and a class with one method for
each operation that the app uses. The clients import `server-only`, so
that only server code, for example a server action or the extension
file of a custom operation, can use them, and the secrets stay on the
server. An answer with an error status throws `ApiError` of
`@/shared/api/third-party`, and each request stops after 10 seconds.

| API | Client | Base URL | Secret |
| --- | ------ | -------- | ------ |
{% for api in ts_apis.values() %}
| `{{ api.name }}` | `{{ api.factory }}()` of `@/shared/api/{{ api.folder }}` | `{{ api.url_env }}` | {{ ("`" ~ api.client_id_env ~ "` (client ID), ") if api.client_id_env }}{{ ("`" ~ api.secret_env ~ "`") if api.secret_env else "None" }} |
{% endfor %}

`{{ (ts_apis.values() | first).factory }}()` reads the settings from the environment, for
example:

```ts
