{% if nextjs.history %}
## Change log

The repositories keep a change log of these entities in the table
`history_entries`: an entry for each create, change, and delete of a
record, with the user, the time, and the old and the new values.

{% for entity_name, entity in definition.entities.items() if entity.history %}
- `{{ entity_name }}`: {% for member in entity.history_members %}`{{ member }}`{{ ", " if not loop.last }}{% endfor %}.
{% endfor %}

`<entity>History` of `@/entities/<entity>` gives the entries of a record
(the access of the read) and a restore (the access of the update). A
restore gives the fields of the entry of a change their old values
back, with the checks of an update, and adds an entry `restored`. A
change outside the repositories adds no entry: SQL in a script, a
delete of the database (`on_delete: cascade`), and the seed.

{% endif %}
